// Title: Non-DLL Extension File Renamed With DLL Extension
// Sigma ID: bbfd974c-248e-4435-8de6-1e938c79c5c1
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-02-19 | Modified: 2023-11-11
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1036.008
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects rename operations of files with non-DLL extensions to files with a DLL extension. This
//   is often performed by malware in order to avoid initial detections based on extensions.
// False positives:
//   - Likely from installers and temporary locations
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/ffforward/status/1481672378639912960
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1036/T1036.md#atomic-test-1---system-file-copied-to-unusual-location
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules-threat-hunting/windows/file/file_rename/file_rename_win_non_dll_to_dll_ext.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath endswith ".dll" and (not((PreviousFileName endswith ".dll" or PreviousFileName endswith ".tmp" or PreviousFileName =~ "" or isnull(PreviousFileName) or (InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains ":\\Windows\\WinSxS\\" and InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\TiWorker.exe") or (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith ":\\Windows\\System32\\wuauclt.exe" or FolderPath contains ":\\$WINDOWS.~BT\\Sources\\") or (InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains ":\\Program Files (x86)\\" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains ":\\Program Files\\")))) and (not(PreviousFileName contains "\\SquirrelTemp\\temp"))
